00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.820
Okay, let's go back the story.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.070
There's this one moment captured on film

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.100
that I can't seem to get out of my mind.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.440
There's a boat sailing the waters

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.650
to the remote island of Iceland in 1938.

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:12.380
There are smiling faces

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.200
and tourists doing what
they've always done

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.430
and will continue to do,

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.140
exploring the vastness of this country.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.170
And then there's shots of
children smiling, playing, living.

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:25.050
It's honestly beautiful footage.

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:26.690
But when you pause this clip

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:29.840
and think about who is the
person holding this camera,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.870
the person zoomed into all
of these kids smiling faces,

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:35.350
these people alive and well,

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.690
the person holding this
camera is Hitler's girlfriend.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:40.410
Her name was Eva Braun.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:43.100
She was the longtime confidant, girlfriend

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.830
and eventual wife of Adolf Hitler.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.240
The only person who could
call him by his name,

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.710
and the one who bit into a
cyanide pill alongside him

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.940
as they both ended their lives together

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.350
in a small study in Berlin,

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:58.470
as Germany was losing the war.

00:01:58.470 --> 00:01:59.750
Oh, and this footage was taken

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:03.080
just a few months before
Hitler invaded Poland

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:05.020
to start the bloodiest war of all time.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.310
So who was she?

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:09.900
And why was she on a tour in Iceland?

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.120
And I guess most importantly,

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.140
what role did Iceland play

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.663
in Hitler's grand plans
to take over the world?

00:02:16.663 --> 00:02:20.163
(upbeat orchestral music)

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.370
Eva Braun met Hitler
while working in Munich

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:41.010
as a model and assistant
to Hitler's photographer.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.950
They got together when
she was 19 and he was 42,

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:47.820
and she remained the
closest person to Hitler

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:50.360
leading up to and during the war.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.640
Eva was a photographer and is responsible

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.480
for many of the images and
film we have of Hitler today.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.730
Hitler wanted to keep
their relationship a secret

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:01.290
because he thought being a bachelor

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:05.350
would like give him a wider
appeal among Germany's women.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:07.520
Okay, big PR guy Hitler was.

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.173
He would always say he
was married to Germany.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.050
Okay, so it's summer 1939,

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:18.730
Hitler is literally two months
away from invading Poland

00:03:18.730 --> 00:03:20.290
and starting world war II.

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:22.400
And Eva is on a Nazi boat

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.010
with this sweet swimming pool on it.

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.750
I want a boat with a swimming pool.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:28.210
And they're traveling to Iceland.

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:31.310
They visit the Geyser
and see all the hot water

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.480
and the steam and the volcanic rocks,

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.420
and they're in Reykjavik.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.150
I mean, this doesn't
look too much different

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:38.370
from my trip in Iceland.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:41.420
Anyway, it turns out
that the Nazi leadership

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.620
was kind of obsessed with Iceland.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:47.030
And not because of the black
sand beaches and glaciers,

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.067
but because of the people.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:51.734
(curious music)

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.630
Specifically, this guy, Henrich Himmler,

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.340
the big dog in the Nazi regime,

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.810
the literal architect of the Holocaust.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:06.670
He was the one who loved Iceland the most.

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:09.330
He loved the Viking lore and legends,

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.730
but he also had this twisted enthusiasm

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.300
for the fact that the
whole country was white.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.560
Icelanders in Himmler's mind,

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.050
were the pure superior Nordic race

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:22.083
that he thought the Nazi
message would resonate with.

00:04:23.135 --> 00:04:23.968
It's insane.

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:26.690
So as the Nazis were
gaining power in Germany,

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.000
they turned to Iceland.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.740
They bought an apartment
in the capital, Reykjavik,

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:33.740
and they sent this guy a Nazi loyalist

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:36.580
who was tasked with being
a diplomat to Iceland.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.840
His job was very simple,

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.570
to commune with the racially
pure Icelandic people

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:46.210
and fulfill Himmler's dream of
converting them to Nazi-ism.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.910
More on how that went
later, but real quick,

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.860
another reason that the
Nazis were so into Iceland

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.370
was because of this.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:55.900
These are the convoy routes between the UK

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.780
and the Northern hemisphere.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:01.540
This is where goods supplies, ammo, troops

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.530
would be moved between the two regions.

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.840
See how these routes
run right past Iceland?

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.958
- [Narrator] 1500 Air miles from Halifax,

00:05:09.958 --> 00:05:11.660
825 miles from Scotland,

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:14.720
and only 900 from Nazi-held Norway.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.510
- The Nazis realized that if
they could take over Iceland

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:19.080
and have a base here,

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.470
it would render this
route way too dangerous.

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:25.820
So yeah, the Nazis were
kind of into Iceland,

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:28.620
not just because of the
racial makeup of the people

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.160
and the abundant resources,

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.300
but also because of the
prime strategic location

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.683
in the impending war.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:36.530
Okay, so let's fast forward

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.600
to a year after Eva
Braun's trip to Iceland.

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.900
It's 1940, the war has started,

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.900
the Nazis have started
conquering their neighbors,

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.470
moving into Denmark,
Norway, and soon Sweden.

00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:52.080
Meanwhile, Iceland is
remaining a neutral country,

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.440
a reminder that remaining
neutral during world war II,

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.630
isn't easy, but anyway,
Iceland is remaining neutral.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:01.770
And the diplomat who the
Nazis had sent to Iceland

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:02.603
is still there,

00:06:02.603 --> 00:06:05.510
he's still working on
recruiting the Icelanders

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:07.240
to the Nazi cause,

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.640
and not having tons of success.

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:11.310
He recruited like a small
group of college kids

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:12.143
to the cause.

00:06:12.143 --> 00:06:15.430
And overall he's kind of
disappointed in Iceland.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:18.330
The place is not what
Himmler thought it was,

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:19.760
but he doesn't tell anyone back home.

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:21.980
He doesn't want to
disappoint the Nazi regime.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.380
Instead he confides in his journal,

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.720
complaining that Iceland's theaters

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.130
perform plays written by Jews

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:32.400
and that they have no
apples in their stores.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:34.720
Like that's her complaint? It's like, oh,

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:36.520
they have no apples in the stores.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:37.900
Like I hate this country.

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:40.890
He also complained that
they held their forks

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:44.150
with their right hands like shovels.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:45.050
Oh gosh.

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:48.780
This was not the aryan in
utopia that he was hoping for.

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.610
But still Iceland had strategic value,

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:53.750
the Nazi army is moving north.

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:56.190
And you know, who's most
freaked out by this,

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.700
by this movement north?

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.360
This guy, Winston Churchill,

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:02.250
leader of the UK at the time.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.087
Churchill said, quote,

00:07:04.087 --> 00:07:08.287
"Whoever possesses Iceland
holds a pistol firmly pointed

00:07:08.287 --> 00:07:11.770
"at England and America and Canada."

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:12.670
Yeah.

00:07:12.670 --> 00:07:14.140
That's pretty much sums it up.

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:16.510
Churchill had been trying
to convince Iceland

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:18.910
to join their side, but Iceland was like,

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:22.130
no, we have a hundred thousand
people. We have no army.

00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.610
We're going to remain neutral.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:25.570
And Churchill becomes impatient.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.200
So in may of 1940,

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:30.130
not even a year after Eva
Braun's getaway to Iceland,

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.830
Churchill sends in his Navy,

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:32.980
they showed up to Iceland

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.790
on a mission called operation fork.

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:37.380
Sort of weird name, but whatever.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:40.190
So the Navy arrives to
the port of Reykjavik,

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:43.190
not to an army, but to a bunch of locals,

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:46.780
like why is there a giant
Navy arriving to our country?

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.830
Remember Iceland doesn't have an army.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:53.520
So they sent the local police
to tell the British Navy

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.270
that they were in violation
of Iceland's sovereignty.

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.550
The British troops were
like, yeah, I know anyway,

00:07:59.550 --> 00:08:01.300
could you tell all these people to move

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.630
so we can dock our boats
and let our Marines off?

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:07.480
And the Icelandic police
were like, yeah, okay, sure.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.800
No conflict, no confrontation.

00:08:09.800 --> 00:08:12.760
The British are politely invading Iceland.

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.070
The most cordial invasion ever.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.470
They did this because
they were freaked out

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.990
that the Nazis would do it first.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:19.540
The first thing they do when they show up

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.010
is go to the German diplomat's house.

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:24.260
They show up in certain
knocking on the door

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:25.870
and they're like, Hey, German diplomat,

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.640
we just invaded Iceland
so that the Nazis can't,

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:29.990
by the way, you're arrested.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.960
And the diplomat from the
other side of the room

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:33.360
literally said, this is a quote,

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.637
he said, "you can't do that,

00:08:35.637 --> 00:08:38.710
"Iceland is a neutral nation in the war."

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:41.227
And the British troops said,
and again, this is a quote,

00:08:41.227 --> 00:08:44.367
"Oh yeah, neutral, like
Denmark was neutral?

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:46.377
"Like Norway was neutral?

00:08:46.377 --> 00:08:48.097
"These were neutral countries too.

00:08:48.097 --> 00:08:49.870
"That didn't stop you guys from invading."

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:51.150
So the diplomat is sitting there

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:52.530
trying to get his furnace to work

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:53.980
so he can burn all these documents

00:08:53.980 --> 00:08:56.630
before the British
break in and arrest him,

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:57.670
which they eventually did.

00:08:57.670 --> 00:08:58.600
When they broke in,

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.490
they found a shrine to
Hitler in his house.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:03.100
He had burned a lot of documents,

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.580
but he didn't burn his diary,

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:05.980
which is why we know this guy

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.640
really actually didn't like Iceland.

00:09:07.640 --> 00:09:10.600
So yeah. Now the British
have troops in Iceland,

00:09:10.600 --> 00:09:13.340
but as the war rages on Britain realizes

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:15.250
that they needed troops elsewhere.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:16.790
They can't afford to have all these troops

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:19.010
just sitting in Iceland as placeholders.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:21.790
So they call upon their
friends, the Americans,

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:22.623
they're like America,

00:09:22.623 --> 00:09:23.760
can you please help us out with troops?

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:25.450
And America is like,
no, we already told you,

00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:27.270
we're not getting involved in the war.

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:29.980
Because at this time America
was not involved in the war.

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:30.880
They were neutral.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:33.210
So Britain is like, okay,
is there a loophole here?

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:37.830
So Britain asks Iceland to
ask America to come help them,

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:40.050
as one neutral nation to another.

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:42.150
America is like, okay cool, I can do that.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:46.350
- [Narrator] Another union,
if not actually have allies,

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.760
then suddenly have two armies
with the same objective

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:51.900
was cemented when American
troops joined ours in Iceland.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.720
- [Narrator 2] With Iceland in his hands,

00:09:53.720 --> 00:09:55.600
Hitler could have
controlled our sea lanes,

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:58.030
but accepting an invitation
and the Icelandic government

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.370
we got there first.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.240
- So before the U.S. ever got

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.260
officially involved in the war,

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:05.830
which happened when Japan
bombed Pearl Harbor,

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:06.740
before all of that,

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:09.160
they sent 25,000 troops to Iceland

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:10.270
to hold down the fort

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:13.460
so that the British troops
could go fight elsewhere.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.399
- [Narrator 2] At first,
the Icelanders didn't take

00:10:15.399 --> 00:10:16.630
to the strange faces and uniforms,

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.600
which began to appear on the street.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:23.550
- I freaking love 1940s
American military documentaries.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:26.007
They're just so, they're just so bizarre.

00:10:26.007 --> 00:10:28.760
- [Narrator 2] Some were steaming
hot and come in very handy

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:32.060
when they want their long
handled johns fresh and dainty

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:33.340
for that Saturday inspection.

00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:34.480
- While in Iceland,

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.590
the Americans start building roads

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:39.770
and bunkers and ports and bases.

00:10:39.770 --> 00:10:41.200
- [Narrator 2] The United States army

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.540
is laying better road beds and is widening

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:44.820
and strengthening the bridges

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.350
to permit the passage of
heavier trucks and tanks.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.980
- This is stuff that is still there today.

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:52.490
A lot of Icelanders
see this as a blessing,

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:54.850
since it helped upgrade
their infrastructure.

00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:56.560
Helped give them like big, beautiful roads

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:57.440
around the country,

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.860
but rightfully so,

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:01.960
many feel like they were used as a pawn

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:05.450
by these super powers that
violated their sovereignty

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:07.870
in the name of geo strategy,

00:11:07.870 --> 00:11:10.180
which is absolutely what happened.

00:11:10.180 --> 00:11:13.050
As always with occupation
it's complicated.

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:13.883
Anyway, but you know what,

00:11:13.883 --> 00:11:15.400
I'm super curious what Icelanders

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.200
actually think about this history.

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:18.800
Was the invasion of Britain

00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:21.370
and the subsequent presidents
of the United States

00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:22.750
a blessing to Iceland?

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:26.610
Or was this a deep violation
of their sovereignty or both?

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:29.670
I'm super curious and
will gladly read comments

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:32.056
from any Icelander who
has thoughts on this.

00:11:32.056 --> 00:11:35.340
(curious music)

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:38.870
So the Americans eventually got
totally involved in the war,

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:42.000
as we know, and they
helped turn the Nazi tide,

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.090
and eventually the allies
defeated the Nazis in Europe.

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:48.510
Hitler and Eva Braun knew
it was coming to an end.

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:50.330
They didn't want to face the justice

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:51.820
that was going to be dealt them

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:54.760
for the atrocities by Hitler's regime.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:57.460
So they took their own
lives in Berlin in 1945,

00:11:57.460 --> 00:11:59.020
as it was all coming to an end.

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:00.010
And that's for Iceland,

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:03.000
the troops eventually left and Icelanders

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:06.320
were sort of done being a
part of this global system

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:08.520
that could just throw
them around like a pawn.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:11.660
They had been a part of the
kingdom of Denmark in some way,

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.350
but right after the war,

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:17.400
they voted 97% to move
away from the Danish crown

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.810
and become totally independent,
an independent Republic,

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:22.050
which is what they are today.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:26.040
And they remain quite neutral
and independent with no army,

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:27.730
no membership in the EU,

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:30.950
and despite the great powers
who tried to persuade them

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.210
and occupy them,

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:36.040
Iceland has retained its
unique and independent culture.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:36.873
A couple of years ago,

00:12:36.873 --> 00:12:39.140
I got to interview the
prime minister of Iceland

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:42.650
when I was making an episode
of Explained for Vox.

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.470
I learned about how
Iceland leads the world

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:48.985
in gender equality, in
happiness, in energy sustainable.

00:12:48.985 --> 00:12:51.652
(upbeat music)

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:58.280
It's a special place

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:00.710
and not because it is
strategically located.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:04.640
I will certainly be back
many times over the years.

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:05.640
Thanks for watching.

